Derived the universal options pricing formula
  from thermodynamic mathematics;
  died before the Nobel Prize was awarded

Opened in the former smoker&rsquo;s lounge of the CBOT;
  traded 911 contracts on Day 1; grew to the world&rsquo;s
  largest options exchange

Publisher of The Options Playbook;
  Overby was Senior Options Analyst;
  TradeKing was later acquired by Ally Financial

Imposed 1977 moratorium on new options listings;
  lifted in 1980 after comprehensive market study;
  shaped modern regulatory framework

Granted SEC license in 1935 to create a stock
  option exchange; didn&rsquo;t act on it until 1968;
  its smoker&rsquo;s lounge became the CBOE

Attempted to create market structure for
  OTC options before exchanges existed;
  advertised in financial journals to find counterparties
